{
  "collections": [
    {
      "description": "Single-tap hopper-game conformance battery for the eval-game-hoppers web app, driven through pagehub-browser at a 390x844 MOBILE viewport. Asserts the 5-pillar DOM contract (instant restart, shareable score, creator-friendly difficulty, zero install friction, payment via ads) + gameplay shape (player species ∈ {kangaroo, rabbit, grasshopper, flea, jerboa}; frog forbidden; data-current-lane increments per tap) + mobile design quality. Three navigations: (A) ?lane-speed=0&lane-density=0&deterministic=1&die-after=6&seed=hop-test-001 — frozen, no spawns, 6 taps -> lane 6 -> game-over; drives pillars 1/2/4/5 + the playing design-audit. (B) ?lane-density=0.5&deterministic=1 — spawns objects frozen at xBase (no drift/collision) so the grader can count the lane-kind cadence (bank for lane<=0; then repeating grass/road/riverbed) and the 3-logs-per-riverbed contract. (C) ?score=6 — shared-score banner. Deterministic mode = no rAF, so all asserts are timing-stable. The ground-truth lane simulator lives in the platform seed. Two design-audit requests (via /evaluate) encode a mobile design review: playing -> playfield fills >=80% of viewport height (no dead band), difficulty-active is PRESENT (pillar-3 contract) but VISUALLY HIDDEN in normal play (sr-only; get-text still reads its textContent so the pillar-3 echo still passes), share is a >=44px tap target; game-over -> ad-close is within the viewport (no scroll needed), >=44px, a death-cause element gives non-empty feedback, play-again is >=44px. 48 items, under the 50 cap.",
      "items": [
        "lifecycle-01-create-session",
        "lifecycle-02-navigate",
        "p4-zero-install-state-playing",
        "p4-no-password-inputs",
        "p4-no-email-inputs",
